## .NET
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
## local `dotnet publish` output (e.g. `dotnet publish src/Cider.Daemon -o ./out|./publish`) —
## never a build artifact worth tracking, wherever it lands.
publish/
publish-fdd/
out/
## (build output only — do NOT use bare [Ll]ogs/ style rules here: they also match
## real source directories such as src/Cider.Core/Logs/ and tests/Cider.Tests/Logs/)
artifacts/
*.user
*.userosscache
*.suo
*.sln.docstates
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.received.*
TestResults/
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
msbuild.log
msbuild.err
msbuild.wrn
*.binlog
.dotnet/
.packages/
nuget.config.user

## macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

## cider runtime artifacts
*.sock
.cider/
## transitional: the pre-rename runtime data dir, ignored until nobody has one left
.apple-demon/

## nitro agent workspace: the JSONL export is the tracker's source of truth in git;
## the SQLite database and its WAL/SHM files are local-only.
.nitro/*
!.nitro/agents/
.nitro/agents/*
!.nitro/agents/tasks.jsonl

## python bytecode from the compat harness
__pycache__/
*.pyc
